---
source: core/src/security/protected_reads/moderate_tests.rs
expression: "explained.expect(\"explained\")"
---
Security level Moderate blocked writing `.git/config`: agent commands always run inside the sandbox, even when you approve them, and the sandbox keeps the project's .git folder (git hooks and config) read-only. Secretless agent launch keeps agent commands inside the sandbox at every security level, so changing the level would not allow it; a person can run the command in their own terminal.
